.TH AM5-SPD-DIAG 1 "2026-08-19" "am5-spd-diag 1.0.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
am5-spd-diag \- AM5 DDR5 SPD hub diagnostics after sleep / warm reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B am5-spd-diag
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures AMD AM5 DIMM/SPD identity across boot, shutdown, and systemd sleep/resume.
Detects firmware-visible SPD hub corruption (Unknown/missing part, 8-bit width,
SPD5118 MR11=0x08) after sleep and a warm reboot.
Sleep policy (deep / s2idle) is never changed.
.PP
Motherboard and DIMM serials are recorded for vendor tickets. System UUID and
asset tags are omitted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Whether SPD identity is healthy as of the last capture, plus live MemTotal.
.TP
.B analyze
Sleep/reboot history, corruption chain, hub evidence.
.B \-\-from
.I FILE
loads a package tarball (or extracted directory) instead of live logs.
.TP
.B open
Open the GTK results window. Optional
.I status
,
.I analyze
,
.I report
, or
.I probe
plus
.B \-\-from
.I FILE
.TP
.B snapshot
Capture DIMM/SPD evidence now. A local active session does not need a
password. Uses the snapshot helper only (no fix).
.TP
.B report
Snapshot, then print ticket markdown and save it. The GTK Report view
uses the last capture and does not snapshot.
.B \-\-from
.I FILE
skips snapshot and reads a package instead. Prints markdown only unless
.B \-\-out
.I FILE
is given.
.TP
.B package
Snapshot, then evidence tarball.
.TP
.B probe
Read MR11 on kernel spd5118 hubs (host SMBus). A local active session
does not need a password.
.TP
.B fix
Experimental in-band MR11 clear. Requires admin authentication. Records a recover timeline event. Does not reboot.
.TP
.B purge
Delete captured logs.
.I /var/log/am5-spd-diag
is removed with systemd-tmpfiles first (needs root); user XDG data is
removed only after that succeeds. Does not uninstall the program.
.PP
A capture that finds current corruption posts a persistent urgent desktop
notification (no timeout). The notice uses the warning emblem as its image
and the application icon from the desktop file. Clicking it opens the GTK
results window on
.BR "am5-spd-diag status"
(or
.BR "am5-spd-diag open" ).
Analyze and Report buttons (on the notice and in the window footer) show
those views. Copy puts the current text on the clipboard. Package writes
an evidence tarball (no extra snapshot) and opens its folder in the file
manager so a ticket can be filed without a terminal. Acting on the
notice closes it with CloseNotification. GNOME can keep those actions
after the sender exits. Other common desktops (Plasma, XFCE, Cinnamon,
MATE, LXQt, dunst) only deliver clicks to the connection that called
Notify, so the sender stays connected until the notice is clicked or
dismissed. SSH/console sessions still get journal and
.BR wall .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/am5-spd-diag
Captures, reports, and packages. systemd-tmpfiles creates this tree as
.B 0755 root:root
(files typically
.BR 0644 ).
Any local user can list and read it; only root can write.
Board and DIMM serials are included. Use
.B package
for a tarball you own.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/am5-spd-diag
User reports and packages when
.I /var/log/am5-spd-diag
is not writable. Default
.IR ~/.local/share/am5-spd-diag .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/am5-spd-diag.conf
Creates and re-owns the system log tree at boot
.RB ( systemd-tmpfiles --create ).
Does not empty the logs on reboot.
.TP
.I /usr/share/am5-spd-diag/tmpfiles-purge.conf
Used only by
.B am5-spd-diag purge
.RB ( systemd-tmpfiles --remove ).
Not installed under
.IR tmpfiles.d .
.TP
.I /etc/am5-spd-diag.conf
Optional overrides.
.SH NOTES
From a source tree, polkit only authorizes the installed helpers
.I /usr/libexec/am5-spd-diag/pkexec-snapshot
,
.I pkexec-probe
, and
.I pkexec-recover
\&. Snapshot and probe are allowed without a password for a local
active session. Fix (GTK Fix) still requires admin authentication.
Install with
.B make build
then
.B sudo make PREFIX=/usr install
or a distro package. The internal
.B capture
subcommand is used by systemd units and is not listed in
.BR \-\-help .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmidecode (8)
